    affiliation: "University of Pernambuco (UPE)"
  - family-names: "Andrade de A. Fagundes"
    given-names: "Roberta"
    affiliation: "University of Pernambuco (UPE)"
repository-code: "https://github.com/halcyondavys/dream-framework"
url: "https://github.com/halcyondavys/dream-framework"
license: MIT
year: 2026
keywords:
  - dynamic ensemble selection
  - ensemble regression
  - heterogeneous ensemble
  - local competence estimation
  - dynamic combination
  - meta-learning
abstract: >
  DREAM is a three-phase framework for dynamic ensemble selection and combination
  applied to regression tasks. Phase 1 performs multicriteria global model selection
  from a heterogeneous pool using a Combined Selection Score (CSS) optimized via
  Bayesian search (Optuna/TPE). Phase 2 estimates local competence for each base
  model using KNN with Inverse Distance Weighting (IDW). Phase 3 applies three
  dynamic combination strategies (DREAM-DS, DREAM-DW, DREAM-DWS) evaluated on
  30 benchmark regression datasets using a 20x10-fold cross-validation protocol.
